hinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The full order went through. I'll confirm the final order list to make sure there's no leftover partial order.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Ccs9ovLu7PNddN9upRsPS5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I placed the order for the new hires as a single purchase order, PO0002, for $1,554, shipping to HQ.\n\n- **3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C docks** (new, $189 each, $567). I used DK-200 rather than the DK-210 successor because it was in stock.\n- **3 \u00d7 MN-27 27-inch 4K monitors** (new, $329 each, $987).\n\nThe order is under the $2,500 threshold, so it didn't need manager approval.\n\nThe first submission timed out and committed only the docks, as PO0001 ($567). I cancelled that partial order, so it shows as cancelled and its charge was refunded. Then I resubmitted the full order, which placed PO0002 with both items. The final order list has no duplicate charge.\n\nThe ship-to address was entered as \"HQ\" because that's all the request specified; the system didn't require a street address.", "type": "text"}]}]}